<title>USA: Vermont voters approve two local bond issues.</title>
<headline>Vermont voters approve two local bond issues.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vermont's voters approved two local bond issues, local officials said, citing preliminary results.</p>
<p>The details for the initiatives are presented in the following list.</p>
<p>--Chelsea, Vt., Approved a $500,000 bond issue to pay for an addition to the Orange County courthouse.</p>
<p>--Montpelier, Vt., Winning margin 2,159 versus 1,480 against. Approved a $400,000 bond issue to pay for rennovations and additions to the Washington County courthouse.</p>
<p>--Joan Gralla, 212-859-1654</p>
